field board.definition_of_done
  provenance: unobjected
  evidence: Drafted by the delivery team 2026-09-15
  value: |
    Builds clean with no new warnings.
    Runs from a fresh folder with only the staged definitions and assets.
    The field's help panel is written: source, why, if-blank, example.
    The record file still round-trips and diffs one line per changed cell.
field board.sprint_goal
  provenance: specified
  evidence: Scope expanded 2026-09-15: "I want a full PM tool, Kanban boards, everything"
  value: |
    Sprint 1: every lifecycle screen usable end to end on this project's own
    record, with the house style applied and record #1 pre-loaded.

    Revised mid-sprint by CR5: the goal is now that a person who has never run
    a project can be walked through one and understand what they just did.
field changes.log
  provenance: specified
  evidence: Raised and decided by the sponsor, 2026-09-15
  row x1
    provenance: specified
    evidence: "yes I want the forms but I want a full PM tool, Kanban boards, everything" (2026-09-15)
    cell change
      value: Expand scope from the Initiating screens (M2) to the full lifecycle, including a sprint board.
    cell decided_by
      value: Nyx (sponsor)
    cell impact
      value: Adds nine screens beyond the two in the M2 handoff. M3 and M4 content delivered early; no milestone date moved. Increases R4, scope creep, which is why it is logged rather than absorbed.
    cell kind
      value: Scope
    cell raised_by
      value: Nyx
    cell raised_on
      value: 2026-09-15
    cell ref
      value: CR1
    cell status
      value: Approved
  row x2
    provenance: specified
    evidence: "name it AutoPM for now" (2026-09-15)
    cell change
      value: Name the product AutoPM, closing the open working-title question.
    cell decided_by
      value: Nyx (sponsor)
    cell impact
      value: Repository, icon, executable and installer all take the name. Marked as provisional, so a later rename is expected and costs one repo rename.
    cell kind
      value: Scope
    cell raised_by
      value: Nyx
    cell raised_on
      value: 2026-09-15
    cell ref
      value: CR2
    cell status
      value: Approved
  row x3
    provenance: specified
    evidence: "make a repo in the lockewerks org, private for now" (2026-09-15)
    cell change
      value: Create a private repository in the Locke-Werks organisation.
    cell decided_by
      value: Nyx (sponsor)
    cell impact
      value: Reverses the M2 handoff line that there would be no repository until the product was named. The name arrived in the same session.
    cell kind
      value: Scope
    cell raised_by
      value: Nyx
    cell raised_on
      value: 2026-09-15
    cell ref
      value: CR3
    cell status
      value: Approved
  row x4
    provenance: specified
    evidence: "make it pretty, use the house style translated into software instead of a webpage" (2026-09-15)
    cell change
      value: Apply the Locke Werks house material language to the application.
    cell decided_by
      value: Nyx (sponsor)
    cell impact
      value: Adds a theme layer and custom-painted chrome. No functional scope change.
    cell kind
      value: Quality
    cell raised_by
      value: Nyx
    cell raised_on
      value: 2026-09-15
    cell ref
      value: CR4
    cell status
      value: Approved
  row x5
    provenance: specified
    evidence: "I want it to walk me through the steps, not just keep track of it for me- it needs to teach me how to be a pm... not be my pm" (2026-09-15)
    cell change
      value: Reframe the product from a recorder with help text into a guided walkthrough that teaches the role, with coaching on the answers.
    cell decided_by
      value: Nyx (sponsor)
    cell impact
      value: Adds a walkthrough mode, a teaching layer in every definition file, and a rule-based coach. The screens and the record are unchanged underneath. This is the largest change so far and it changes what the product is, not just what it contains.
    cell kind
      value: Scope
    cell raised_by
      value: Nyx
    cell raised_on
      value: 2026-09-15
    cell ref
      value: CR5
    cell status
      value: Approved
field changes.process
  provenance: agreed
  evidence: Follows the charter approval rule, 2026-09-15
  value: |
    Anything that moves a milestone date, adds a screen, or changes what the
    product is goes to the sponsor. Wording, layout and colour inside an approved
    screen do not.

    I am both PM and sponsor on this project, so the discipline is writing the
    change down, not routing it to someone else.
field charter.approval
  provenance: specified
  evidence: "charter approved" (2026-09-15)
  value: Approved by the sponsor, 2026-09-15.
field charter.approval_requirements
  provenance: specified
  evidence: "he does a review when i think we are done, and he tells me if it is right or not" (2026-09-15)
  value: |
    I accept each milestone. Acceptance means I used the screen on this project
    and understood every field.

    Final review by Archon, once, when I think we are done. His verdict decides
    whether the product is right.
field charter.budget
  provenance: agreed
  evidence: "yes to all proposals" (2026-09-15)
  value: $0 beyond existing subscriptions and hosting.
field charter.business_case
  provenance: agreed
  evidence: Summary approved with "yes to all proposals" (2026-09-15)
  value: |
    I do PM work by intuition and want to understand how it fits into a PM job,
    which I am actively pursuing. No existing tool I have holds project-level
    truth: charter, scope, decisions, risks, and status against a plan.

    ProjectMan tracks git state. MemoryBook holds memory and loops. Neither holds
    project intent.
field charter.decision_rule
  provenance: specified
  evidence: My rule from 2026-08-27 about decisions attributed without evidence
  value: |
    Three states: specified (I said it, quote it), agreed (I approved a summary),
    unobjected (proposed, no reply). Only specified and agreed are decisions.

    Every entry in this tool carries one of those states plus an evidence line.
field charter.description_deliverables
  provenance: specified
  evidence: "I want this to be personal installable software- like... project man" (2026-09-15)
  value: |
    Personal, installable desktop software covering the full project lifecycle.
    Each person runs their own install.

    Screens: charter, stakeholder register, requirements, scope and WBS, schedule,
    risk register, sprint board, change log, issues and decisions, status reports,
    closeout.
field charter.exit_criteria
  provenance: specified
  evidence: "exit criteria approved" (2026-09-15)
  value: |
    Close: M5 reached and all four success criteria met.
    Cancel or re-charter: no screen used on a real project for 30 days, or the
    build pulls time off paid PM work for more than two weeks running.
field charter.high_level_requirements
  provenance: agreed
  evidence: "yes to all proposals" (2026-09-15)
  value: |
    Guided input forms for each lifecycle artifact.
    Built-in explanation for each field.
    Decision log with a source field (my own).
    Hybrid structure: predictive phases, with sprints inside Executing.
field charter.key_stakeholders
  provenance: specified
  evidence: "Archon may use it, but he will definately review it" (2026-09-15)
  value: |
    Sponsor, PM and primary user: me.
    Final reviewer: Archon, one review, with the verdict on whether it is right.
    Delivery team: builds from my handoffs.

    Details on the Stakeholder Register screen.
