field risks.register
  provenance: agreed
  evidence: Risk register from the project record, 2026-09-15
  row r1
    provenance: agreed
    evidence: Revised 2026-09-15 after the purpose was reframed to learning
    cell category
      value: Quality
    cell impact
      value: High
    cell owner
      value: Nyx
    cell probability
      value: Medium
    cell ref
      value: R1
    cell response
      value: Every field names its source in the standard and uses industry vocabulary, so what I learn transfers to Jira, Asana and MS Project.
    cell response_type
      value: Mitigate
    cell risk
      value: Because the tool is my own design, I may learn the tool instead of the job it is modelled on, which would leave me no better prepared for a PM role.
    cell status
      value: Open
  row r2
    provenance: agreed
    cell category
      value: Scope
    cell impact
      value: Medium
    cell owner
      value: Nyx
    cell probability
      value: Medium
    cell ref
      value: R2
    cell response
      value: AutoPM holds project intent only. Git state stays in ProjectMan; the boundary is written into the charter.
    cell response_type
      value: Mitigate
    cell risk
      value: Because I already run ProjectMan, MemoryBook and MindTether, a fourth tracker may split where the truth lives.
    cell status
      value: Watching
  row r3
    provenance: specified
    evidence: My rule from 2026-08-27
    cell category
      value: Quality
    cell impact
      value: Medium
    cell owner
      value: Nyx
    cell probability
      value: High
    cell ref
      value: R3
    cell response
      value: Three-state source tag plus an evidence line on every field and every row. Only specified and agreed count as decisions.
    cell response_type
      value: Mitigate
    cell risk
      value: Because decisions get summarised, they may be attributed to me without evidence, which makes the record untrustworthy.
    cell status
      value: Closed
  row r4
    provenance: agreed
    cell category
      value: Scope
    cell impact
      value: High
    cell owner
      value: Nyx
    cell probability
      value: High
    cell ref
      value: R4
    cell response
      value: Explicit out-of-scope list in the charter, and every expansion goes through the change log. CR1 is the first one.
    cell response_type
      value: Mitigate
    cell risk
      value: Because a full PM suite is large, scope may creep until the project never finishes.
    cell status
      value: Open
  row r5
    provenance: agreed
    evidence: Revised 2026-09-15 when the review was defined as a single gate
    cell category
      value: Schedule
    cell impact
      value: High
    cell owner
      value: Nyx
    cell probability
      value: Medium
    cell ref
      value: R5
    cell response
      value: Proposed: review after M4, inside the slack before October 15, and give him the charter up front. Not yet answered.
    cell response_type
      value: Mitigate
    cell risk
      value: Because Archon reviews once at the end, anything he finds wrong surfaces at the most expensive moment, and his availability is outside my control.
    cell status
      value: Open
  row r6
    provenance: agreed
    cell category
      value: Technical
    cell impact
      value: Medium
    cell owner
      value: Nyx
    cell probability
      value: Medium
    cell ref
      value: R6
    cell response
      value: Accepted knowingly. The help panel is the counterweight: if I cannot explain a field from its panel, that is the signal.
    cell response_type
      value: Accept
    cell risk
      value: Because the front end of the schedule is aggressive, architecture decisions get made fast, which works against me understanding every field.
    cell status
      value: Watching
field risks.thresholds
  provenance: agreed
  evidence: Agreed with the charter risk posture, 2026-09-15
  value: |
    Any risk to the October 15 closeout date gets acted on. Anything that only
    costs rework is watched.

    If the build starts pulling time from paid PM work for more than two weeks
    running, that is an exit condition, not a risk.
